{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6192bf8302a20700d883f8e27bea46437d6551e0edf9af2f3e111980a50fd0aa","digest":{"component_or_area":"core configuration and authentication composition framework (RP-04 epic)","key_entities":["OperationSnapshot","PydanticAIRunner","ProviderSession","GitRuntime","LLMRuntime","BridgeRuntime","REBAR_ROOT","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW","SecretStr","SecretBytes","check_config_reads.py","ADR 0098","RP-01","op-cert","AST ownership gate"],"problem_keywords":["operation-scoped configuration","provider authentication composition","credential lifecycle","configuration precedence","ambient state reloading","authorization boundaries","static secrets","provider-native auth"],"propositions":["Configuration and credentials are resolved inconsistently across multiple authorities (LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, observability, op-cert) during a single operation, causing mid-operation behavior changes and unintended identity fallbacks.","Backends reread ambient state after receiving explicit configuration, and authentication composition discards explicit choices or exposes static credentials to unrelated child processes.","An immutable, serializable, non-secret OperationSnapshot must be resolved once per operation boundary with strict precedence (explicit input > environment > project config > user config > schema default) and must remain unchanged for the duration of the operation.","Provider-native authentication and session bindings must be injected only through existing RP-01 ProviderSession builders, preserving budget, retry history, caching, exhaustion semantics, artifacts, tracing, usage, and failure translation without arbitrary client injection.","Static credentials must use Pydantic SecretStr/SecretBytes carriers revealed only in sending adapters, with no universal secret broker or central credential union, and must not appear in repr, equality, serialization, snapshots, logs, or subprocess environment.","Op-cert must accept exactly one of REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH or REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY, validate before service creation, store in a process-owned 0700 directory with 0600 file permissions, and remove runtime SSM/boto3/region coupling."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787382461231447951,"uuid":"f0397602-0878-42fc-915f-c6c2dd97bbaf"}